{"baseRefName":"main","body":"Complete counterexample to the universal nonzero quantum-invariant magnitude claim: at SU(5) WZW level5 (shifted level10), L(5,1) and L(5,2) both have fundamental groupZ/5, while their squared normalized magnitudes are3475+1550sqrt(5) and4025+1800sqrt(5). Both are nonzero. Includes the unchanged exact cyclotomic proof and author receipt plus a separate source/normalization audit and structurally independent five-term root-lattice Gauss-sum proof with2,005exact checks. Intended claimed_solved2/5; novelty unestablished, no human peer-review claim. Parent coordinates the queue entry. No claim against the known SU(2) lens-space theorem.","headRefOid":"6534ad01e519c719628a18984b108e73cf2e8ead","isDraft":true,"mergeable":"UNKNOWN","number":95,"state":"OPEN","title":"SU(5): independently reviewed lens-space counterexample to Conjecture 7.5","url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/95"}
